# Kling voice bind guardrails

## Two different operations (never conflate)

| Operation | Command / UI | Changes voice_id? | Daily use? |
|-----------|--------------|-------------------|------------|
| **Pose re-register** | Beat Gen **Add to Element**; CLI `--refresh-poses-only` | **No** — keeps locked `kling_voice_id` | Yes |
| **Voice refresh** | CLI `--refresh-voice --confirm-voice-overwrite` | **Yes** — new create-voice clone | Rare |

`create-voice` is **non-deterministic**: the same good `kling_voice_samples/*.mp3` can mint a bad clone. Never `--refresh-voice` to debug a single bad beat — compare to a known-good beat first (e.g. beat 18 vs 27).

## Dependency order (implementation)

1. `kling_voice_bind.py` — `voice_bind_history`, archive, rollback, drift detection, create-voice candidate validation
2. `setup_all_kling_character_voices.py` — separate flags; `--confirm-voice-overwrite` required for voice refresh
3. `setup_character_voice()` — archive before overwrite; reject bad create-voice candidates before registry write
4. O3 submit — `VOICE_BIND_DRIFT` when registry `kling_voice_id` ≠ beat's last approved `o3_element_quality` (unless `accept_voice_drift`)

## Operator recovery

```bash
# Roll back to previous working bind (after bad voice refresh)
doppler run -- env MN_PROD_ROOT=<Dropbox/Production> \
  python3 scripts/setup_all_kling_character_voices.py --rollback-voice --char Lorelai
```

Listen to `kling_voice_samples/<char>.mp3` before any voice refresh. After refresh, A/B one known-good beat before redoing others.

## Do not regress

- `add_element_pose()` must continue to pass **existing** `kling_voice_id` into `register_kling_element`.
- Voice refresh must **archive** the active bind to `voice_bind_history` before overwrite.
- Never run voice refresh without `--confirm-voice-overwrite` when status is active.
